592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186083203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186083204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1031 "Dividing Polynomials Using Synthetic Division" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1033 728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051061 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7de546e1-10a1-5134-abfc-9fe21121e7cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186427378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186122678 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b55f74a2-418f-5fce-b67f-29118bc0950f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124331 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5486" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124331 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda$ of the matrix \n![](images/45/4549ab32dddcf46e297a3238d71a51657bbcf5fa1c4b2659000c023fff6f938d.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124331 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b2fcf5d-0da3-5676-b4c6-54095c3fb45c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124331 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/99/99bf36b6acbdd21ab16ca6b434122fed7c474103f6e88ec5688261d5848d542c.svg)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 9-\\lambda  & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )(9-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +9)(\\lambda -9)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda_1=-9,$ $\\lambda_2=9,$ and $\\lambda_3=6.$ \n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124332 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124332 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues ![](images/98/98a445be63a324ba80515c96b7f891797392bdeafb375acb75ce1613f4475d4c.svg) of the matrix \n![](images/f1/f1bc09a8e52ccd286aa0e28fee7f60b17b48ce7423eb897269ab9fda387a93dc.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124332 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76c52a74-9b98-5df5-ac63-64e92af1a580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124332 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix ![](images/da/da1b043be21ae49536ac74a7c5df40af321f327b25fce325a54d87bca7bdd804.svg)\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/0c/0ced5cb154bbec90b1d0832ac1e2bf9e0b3599d4675784a47b32f69861b63549.svg)\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by ![](images/7d/7db7ee38ff2ad420ad85266b4684a9092ca4976b0a312043cdcb40f755f87312.svg) \n\nExpanding the determinant across the ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg)st row, we get the following:\n\n![](images/8a/8a07ee34efc93d9c0454d7275b94f5dcd303a938784b797a265eba29356f5801.svg)\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of ![](images/22/225eed5110c60c0ca4c2205a24ba280024533de3e65ad4d32fae9617ce06b4a9.svg) \n![](images/04/04cd74c64ddaedf3b73761d8098979ac86cd9089751a10278b9aedd2bc8f98dc.svg)\n\nLet's pick ![](images/96/9656fb92a4f17a34456f345565f0e7d85fd432d9cd38070cdada71e52647529c.svg) Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n![](images/5d/5d2e25abee3cc05da3b3a83482899c4b6558fd54a4d66e39331ba1b55f50a917.svg)\nSo, ![](images/0a/0a68ef90ceec4971dc74a1a73e0a5bbdee3eec5956ddbce404a48517b2828059.svg) is a root of the equation. This means we can factor ![](images/ff/ffad613e6c3731c1406a83b447c4212d48bc41005ca7817a73d5c2ed66f79b30.svg) out of ![](images/03/0367fad967f1c2089ceaefb337b32b0a39b425dd3f0f900ec7b859547a036a89.svg) using synthetic division:\n\n| ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/0c/0cf2eee0cdec31b7acdc244a255aaee7d6d520cfeee67b64ac9cf215f5377477.svg) | ![](images/f1/f1557a7d98a910797c6117a185f64b753b0ebcd56db3f187aca1952f4f38df5c.svg) | ![](images/8e/8ec9094ad8c9b7c6e3da424099eca8e856a690c4355d4af8210da28f495a72f0.svg) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | ![](images/11/113a2e06675ede52bfef4b9178bf4e7820332c07c597cb963b36a5bbef55f6cf.svg) | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/37/37e17c4a2302e6352fb7186621c9c43bb5e99d43a8a0bc700c0181d36c6cc915.svg) | ![](images/46/46908fb7561d19927fe58a38ab26cba3ff8a35cf75cc0da234f08773dc991398.svg) |\n|  | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/37/37e17c4a2302e6352fb7186621c9c43bb5e99d43a8a0bc700c0181d36c6cc915.svg) | ![](images/46/46908fb7561d19927fe58a38ab26cba3ff8a35cf75cc0da234f08773dc991398.svg) | ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n![](images/d8/d802c5d6ff81a500a8d7d00ec9e20daafb07d355a1ce0d9a0b48dc03a88088c9.svg)\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ![](images/19/191f231d4e62c28931ed18cf133acb0e0ec66e845af743409198c4420953bd52.svg) ![](images/eb/eb3981cb149c9d1b26c2b87bd92a5aef5ead1787d8cb817fa3c1efd6a66074f9.svg) and ![](images/e9/e988f1ab98136f2d888e83baf436d8f659654a55eb2d2b3e11029b365a52c6e0.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124380 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7047" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124380 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/2e/2e17e4fa743f6f8d3f5987b9095cf6976ae8eadf36ee4456ea8a9195201526e4.svg)\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda=4$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nII. $\\lambda=-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda=6$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124380 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1c51187-c0a6-505c-bc58-2319b439086e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124380 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\, P-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/38/38316eff018e61b4f9f6ce90e0e231ed1eeb6fe993f3b107a5ad8057e3641fd4.svg)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(P-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4 \\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3 \\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-\\lambda )\\cdot (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 7 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )((-1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-35) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda=3,$ $\\lambda=4,$ $\\lambda=6,$ and $\\lambda=-6$ (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124522 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124523 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186125062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124571 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1045 "The Characteristic Equation of a Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186125406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1050 1080.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124749 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9ba6f288-55b6-582e-8aa1-d15ec442bd9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125013 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186122678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125013 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125013 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125013 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125013 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f39262c6-06ce-51e6-92a2-5f2acfb813a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125013 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3-\\lambda  \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -3)+2(2\\lambda -2)-3(2\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda )+(4\\lambda -4)-(6\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125406 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125406 #edb/ref 1061 20093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125406 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f05d37d-484a-5ae0-8ed9-0b46584f4a7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125406 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125407 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125407 #edb/ref 1061 20094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125407 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9edf1314-60a8-581e-afc3-f39ecd8b7951" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125407 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125408 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125408 #edb/ref 1061 20095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125408 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "37883812-d28d-5bd5-97af-2df4b9f73f66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125408 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125409 #edb/ref 1061 20096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125409 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d8240de1-8637-5d84-886a-269d69011445" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125409 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125488 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125488 #edb/ref 1061 25951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125488 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c9b6469-fe8d-5b75-bb95-efbf2684e9ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125488 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125785 #edb/ref 1064 "We can find the eigenvalues of a $3\\times 3$ matrix in much the same way as for $2\\!\\times\\! 2$ matrices. \n\nRemember, $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $A$ if $A\\mathbf{v} = \\lambda\\mathbf{v}$ for some non-zero vector $\\mathbf{v}$. This implies that the equation\n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\mathbf{v}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nhas a non-trivial solution, which means that the matrix $A-\\lambda I$ is singular, and consequently\n$\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.$\nTherefore, if we want to find the eigenvalues of a $n\\!\\times\\! n$ matrix $A,$ we have to find the solutions of the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.\n$$\n\nLet's go through this process in the case of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n![](images/21/21e0994519fbba32a84020ce4661e98600c1307947083ddc3afe9902658143c1.svg)\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix $A-\\lambda I{:}$\n\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\lambda \\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set and solve the characteristic equation $\\,\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ Using the fact that the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the elements on the main diagonal, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )(-8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +8)(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are $\\lambda=-2,$ $\\lambda=-8,$ and $\\lambda=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125785 #edb/ref 1065 3564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125785 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "535c5b8b-f815-5ded-8ae5-668bac420af7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125785 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125786 #edb/ref 1064 "The **algebraic multiplicity** of an eigenvalue $\\lambda$ is the number of times it is a solution of the characteristic equation. \n\nFor example, consider a $6\\times 6$ matrix $A$ with the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n(\\lambda-{\\color{red}4})(\\lambda-{\\color{red}4})(\\lambda-1)(\\lambda+8)^{\\color{blue}3} =0\n$$\n\nThe eigenvalue $\\lambda={\\color{red}4}$ is a double root. Therefore, it has algebraic multiplicity $2.$ \n\nBy the same reasoning, we say that \n\n- $\\lambda=1$ has algebraic multiplicity $1,$ and\n\n- $\\lambda=-8$ has algebraic multiplicity $\\color{blue}3$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125786 #edb/ref 1065 3565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125786 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "db18f185-0dce-547f-95f2-71b60a6d4d2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125786 #edb/ref 1067 "The Algebraic Multiplicity of an Eigenvalue" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321174 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-53\\lambda -36=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321174 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321174 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02fadbdc-d540-572d-a6fc-e90b0bea45aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321329 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321329 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321329 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "16474b71-dd87-5c02-90a1-1986cdcc2b44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321371 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -108=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321371 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321371 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d8b6827-a8f5-5e9e-a456-3c1f4b0bd806" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321696 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +1)=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321696 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321696 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "455b312d-436f-5a59-beed-3c43b768e4a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321806 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda +72=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321806 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321806 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "53cbf2a7-4b85-5a35-aa42-5f47e5014747" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321840 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321840 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321840 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5844cdec-8e7d-5d66-a293-f8b40e411e1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322336 #edb/ref 1080 "\\lambda (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +2)=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322336 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322336 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9521fe4a-7fce-5da7-a5cc-1b5de6565706" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322392 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322392 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322392 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9e18c66c-1798-5646-b90c-5aa3dcdc792b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322498 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+53\\lambda +36=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322498 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322498 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ac8c4ccf-02d4-5b71-8706-613880e25eb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322987 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322987 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322987 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eb00f264-ac0e-52cf-bbb6-b0d74f11988e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186322392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323175 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "05b0b363-ceb3-501c-b8ad-22246e96a7de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186321840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323203 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "11bd07c2-d426-5569-a039-db8a048a82ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323857 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323857 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36860" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323857 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323857 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323857 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a91b44ac-1def-566a-a0ac-b4f797a0bab1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323857 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd column, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(-2)(-2)) & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323911 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323911 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323911 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323911 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323911 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04cda9cf-e19f-5987-86a4-1bd75a963670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323911 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ 1 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-9|\\begin{aligned}0 & -8 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8)-9(-16) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+37\\lambda -72)+144 & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+37\\lambda +72 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366006 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366006 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37387" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366006 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366006 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $C$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C$\n\nII. $\\lambda =5$ is an eigenvalue of $C$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda =5$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366006 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e41ff16d-c666-5918-91e3-4e187ca2af95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366006 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(C-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $4$th column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-\\lambda )\\cdot (5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ -5 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )^{2}\\cdot ((2-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )+20) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)^{2}({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +14) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D<0$ for the polynomial ${\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +14$ we have that the only real eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5$ (with algebraic multiplicity $2$). \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186366009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366007 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cfcd45ad-3392-56d7-9f7a-f558cdf77f96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366008 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366008 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366008 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9fca3927-3f6f-5b44-b4b9-d2ba4ecdca76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366009 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366009 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366009 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e6b39b02-0c43-5154-abf8-74818045d6f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366010 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366010 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366010 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5de737fa-c3ea-5d82-bb67-a96903882581" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366011 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366011 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366011 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a8a00a64-39c3-55cd-9978-fe5453d5a40d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366012 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366012 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366012 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08349bc9-dea7-5693-842f-2e153b69045e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366365 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366365 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366365 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366365 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda =0$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nII. $\\lambda =-14$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366365 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6753a04-a08e-5bc2-a11a-2cad03fb8d3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366365 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2-\\lambda )\\cdot (-14-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-14-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +14)\\lambda (\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =2,$ $\\lambda =-2,$ $\\lambda =0,$ and $\\lambda =-14$  (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366367 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366370 #edb/r