] [17592186427382 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ed7b9e7c-c2fe-5559-be97-bb8125d6fa51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427383 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{3}-2\\lambda -2=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427383 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427383 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f431214a-fe2c-58fb-acc6-9d70412cfbb8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186427374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427384 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0da5b7ce-3185-5f7f-9a0f-797454d122c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427385 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427385 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427385 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427385 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427385 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ffb7e93-f33c-5adf-acf0-f55e6fbbb059" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427385 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=1.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
